<title>USA: U.S. rig count down 3 to 815 in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. rig count down 3 to 815 in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of rigs exploring for oil and natural gas in the United States stood at 815 as of January 24, down three from the prior week and 112 above the year-ago total of 703, Baker Hughes Inc reported.</p>
<p>The number of rigs drilling on land remained at 685, while rigs working offshore fell three to 107. The number of rigs active in inland waters remained 23.</p>
<p>Among the individual states, the biggest changes occurred in Texas, which was up 11, Ohio, which was down seven and Louisiana, which was down five.</p>
<p>The Gulf of Mexico was 101.</p>
</text>
